Description: design and print labels on label printers
 Tavletta designs labels with text, images, symbols and codes, shows them
 exactly as they will be printed and prints them over the network or USB:
 on label printers with endless tape or die-cut labels, and on office
 printers, one label per page or on label sheets. It talks to each printer
 in its own language.
 .
 Supported printers include the Brother VC-500W, Brother QL and P-touch,
 cab EOS, SQUIX and MACH, NIIMBOT, printers with ZPL, EPL2, TSPL, ESC/POS
 or DYMO LabelWriter, and any printer the system knows through CUPS or IPP.
 .
 Features: QR, Data Matrix, PDF417, Aztec, EAN, UPC and GS1 codes; over
 7000 symbols; label sheets such as Avery or Zweckform; serial labels from
 CSV, ODS or XLSX files; shipping labels from a carrier's PDF; a command
 line that prints without a window, and a print server with a REST API
 and MCP.
 .
 The print server as a system service is in tavletta-server.

Package: tavletta-server
Architecture: all
Depends:
 systemd | systemd-standalone-tmpfiles,
 tavletta (= ${binary:Version}),
 ${misc:Depends},
Description: print server of the Tavletta label designer, as a system service
 Tavletta designs and prints labels on label printers (Brother, cab, Zebra,
 DYMO, NIIMBOT and printers with ZPL, EPL2, TSPL or ESC/POS) and office
 printers.
 .
 This package runs its print server, with a REST API and MCP, as the
 system service tavletta-server: as the user tavletta (made by the
 package), sandboxed, on 127.0.0.1:8790, with its printers and access
 tokens in /etc/tavletta and the labels in /var/lib/tavletta/labels. It is
 installed but neither enabled nor started.
